n</span></span><br>\r\n<span xss=removed><span xss=removed>GREEN = Sufficient CO2</span><br>\r\n<span xss=removed>YELLOW = Danger! Too much CO2. Reduce CO2 injection immediately</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed> </span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed>When the test solution is just added, the color of the test solution will change gradually according to the concentration of CO2</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed>It usually takes several hours. If the color is blue all the time, please increase the CO2 supply and observe it for several hours until it reaches green</span></span><span xss=removed><span xss=removed>. At this time, the CO2 concentration is appropriate.</span></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed> </span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><strong><span xss=removed><span xss=removed>Reminder:</span></span></strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed><span xss=removed>Color is a slow gradual process. It is suggested that the amplitude of CO2 outgassing should not exceed 50% of the outgassing amount each time, so as to avoid excessive hypoxia of fish and shrimp</span></span></span></span></span></p>\r\n',0,'1',0.056,12.2,8.8,3.6,10,7,'25','1','1','2','16135672618722CO2_Bubble_Counter_for_Plant.jpg','16135672618722CO2_Bubble_Counter_for_Plant1.jpg','16135672618722CO2_Bubble_Counter_for_Plant2.jpg','16135672618722CO2_Bubble_Counter_for_Plant3.jpg','16135672618722CO2_Bubble_Counter_for_Plant4.jpg','16135672618722CO2_Bubble_Counter_for_Plant5.jpg','16135672618722CO2_